            <div xml:id="d386-a1">

                <pb facs="0538" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg436"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to Consul Livingston.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Several of our consuls and consular agents
                    have requested instructions as to what is to be the practice of the American
                    consulates in Haiti regarding the acceptance of persons who are being pursued
                    for the so-called political offenses.</p>
                <p>That there might be no misunderstanding I requested the State Department at
                    Washington for positive instructions relative to this matter of asylum, and
                    under date of April 11, 1908, I have been instructed by the Department as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>“Now that the American legation and consulates have been cleared of refugees, you
                    will make it distinctly known that no more Haitian refugees will be admitted to
                    shelter by you or by your subordinates and that no pretext will be afforded for
                    reawakening the question of asylum so far as the Government of the United States
                    is concerned.”</p>
                <p>You are directed to take particular note of these instructions and to see that
                    they are carried out in so far as your office is concerned.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
